Lia (support): FYI customer AcmeHR reports repeated parse failures when using structured/json mode for a batched items response. Ticket #7321.
Sam (eng): Can you paste the exact request + failing response? Also which model/version and API params they used?
Lia (support): Sent repro below from customer. Model: redwood-2. Params: structured_output=true, schema provided.
Lia (support): ```
POST /v1/generate
{
  "model": "redwood-2",
  "structured_output": true,
  "schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "results": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["id", "score"],
          "properties": {
            "id": {"type": "string"},
            "score": {"type": "number"},
            "details": {"type": "object"}
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "prompt": "Return a JSON object with key results: an array of items (id, score, details)."
}
```
Lia (support): Customer got HTTP 200 with body that fails parse on their side: JSONDecodeError and partial objects.
Lia (support): ```
{
  "results": [
    {"id": "a1", "score": 0.92, "details": {}},
    "unexpected string entry",
    {"score": 0.50, "details": {"note": "missing id"}, "extra_key": "foo"}
  ]
}
```
Sam (eng): Thanks. Looks like two separate issues: 1) array contains a raw string item, 2) third object missing required id and has an extra key. Any logs on Redwood side (parse/validation) or did we pass through raw text?
Maria (qa): I repro'ed locally with a short prompt. The model sometimes emits partial items when beam/diverse generation continues after a closing bracket. Repro steps: minimal prompt + schema above + seed. I captured token stream where after the first object generation the model emits a plain token (a punctuation or text) instead of starting a new object.
Maria (qa): Example token stream snippet: `..., "results": [ { "id": "a1", "score": 0.92 }, \n unexpected string entry \n { "score": 0.5 ...`
Eli (cs): Customer says their JSON parser fails (they can't recover). This is blocking their pipeline. Any suggested immediate workaround we can give them?
Sam (eng): Short-term: tell them to enable our `enforce_schema=true` server-side validation flag (if they turn it on the server will return 400 with a clear schema error instead of passing broken JSON). Also suggest setting `max_tokens` to smaller chunk sizes and `stop` to the closing `]}` to reduce trailing stray tokens.
Maria (qa): Workaround verified: with `enforce_schema` enabled, the call returns 400 + body: `{ "error": "SchemaValidationError: results[1]: expected object, got string" }` — much friendlier for client.
Sam (eng): Root cause hypothesis: regression in post-processing patch that tried to be permissive with partial arrays to allow minor free-text interleaving. That permissiveness accidentally lets non-object tokens slip into array elements for strict schema arrays.
Sam (eng): I'll open an emergency PR to tighten the structured output post-processor to re-run schema enforcement before emitting final payload (reject instead of sanitizing).
DeployBot: Canary deploy scheduled: canary-2026-03-17T16:15Z -> rolling patch to structured-output postprocessor.
Eli (cs): Can we ask support to notify AcmeHR about the workaround and ETA for fix? They want to know if we can avoid a code change on their side.
Lia (support): Pinged customer with workaround (enforce_schema=true) and gave ETA ~2 hours for patch to reach hosted. They've switched to enforce_schema and it stopped failing.
Sam (eng): Patch merged to main, canary looks good (no regressions on regression suite). Rolling to prod now.
DeployBot: Rollout complete at 2026-03-17T18:02Z.
Lia (support): Customer confirmed production calls succeed and parser no longer hits partial objects. Closing ticket after 24h confirmation. :thumbsup:
Maria (qa): Adding unit test that simulates interleaved non-object tokens in arrays and asserts we return a validation error rather than emit broken payload.
Sam (eng): Follow-up action: add metric for `structured_validation_rejections` so we can alert when we start passing broken schema again.
Eli (cs): Noted for customer success playbook: recommend `enforce_schema` or client-side defensive parsing until customers can rely on strict server validation.
Lia (support): Closing notes saved to ticket #7321: root cause: permissive post-processing allowed extra/partial array entries. Fix: stricter enforcement; workaround: enforce_schema=true.
